    },
    "committer": {
     "name": "Contributor",
     "email": "dev@example.com",
     "date": "2026-08-24T18:45:58Z"
    },
    "message": "fix(desktop): wire launch reconciliation, close watcher, tray gating, GUI errors\n\n- Reconcile start-at-login with the OS registration right after the singleton lock is acquired (the admin API's documented launch-time contract); best-effort with a warning on failure.\n- Watch window is_open True->False edges (_poll_window_transition/_watch_window_close daemon); survived closes route through handle_window_closed(), app-ending closes stop the tray.\n- Quit path closes the window without recording window_open=False, matching the preserve-window contract.\n- tray_enabled=false gates start-at-login at reconciliation; semantic documented in set_tray_enabled/apply_tray_registration/set_start_at_login docstrings and the dashboard settings help text.\n- Surface DesktopError from the gui-subsystem entrypoint via ctypes MessageBoxW on win32, stderr fallback elsewhere, exiting non-zero.\n- Refuse cleanly on Linux-with-display instead of crashing on the pystray import.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
